aes_n_flask -- encrypt files with AES in a Flask web app
========================================================

This is the main part of my school cryptography project.  I started
working on it in May 2022 (8th school grade) and presented it in March
2023.  It is written in Python with the Flask framework.

Requirements
------------

Python 3 and the packages in requirements.txt (Flask, waitress,
Werkzeug and pycryptodome).  setup_dev.sh creates a virtual environment
in venv/ and installs them there.

Using it
--------

Clone the repository, then start src/app.py with a secret key made of
random letters as its argument:

    git clone https://github.com/mb6ockatf/aes-n-flask.git
    cd aes-n-flask
    python3 src/app.py RANDOM-LETTERS

The app starts on 127.0.0.1.

Reporting bugs
--------------

Report bugs at https://github.com/mb6ockatf/aes-n-flask/issues.

